<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Seiyun</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Say'un</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Seiyun is a town in the Wadi Hadramawt in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yemen">Yemen</a>. It was the capital of the Kathiri sultans, whose large white mud-brick palace still stands in the town and now houses a museum. It lies between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shibam">Shibam</a> and Tarim on the main route through the valley.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/seiyun.jpg" alt="Seiyun" width="320" height="200" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: JialiangGao www.peace-on-earth.org · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sultan_Al_Kathiri_Palace_Seiyun_Yemen.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
